cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Canada LNG Expansion: Lifecycle Emissions Model"
message: >-
  If you use this model, its outputs or its asset register, please cite it
  using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Toronto Climate Observatory"
    city: Toronto
    region: Ontario
    country: CA
abstract: >-
  An open, reproducible model of the greenhouse gas emissions caused by
  Canada's liquefied natural gas export expansion. Covers every LNG asset in
  the country in the register - operating, under construction and proposed -
  over a per-asset, per-calendar-year lifecycle panel, with an explicit
  carbon dioxide and methane split, territorial tagging (Canada, international
  marine bunkers, foreign), and monetised global loss and damage at Canada's
  official social cost of greenhouse gases. Headline results are the export
  chain.
keywords:
  - liquefied natural gas
  - lifecycle emissions
  - methane
  - social cost of carbon
  - loss and damage
  - Canada
license: CC-BY-4.0
